 @captainmorgan2530  $70 today is still more than $60 2 years ago and games have been getting worse and worse. I'm old enough to remember when this all started with people saying I'm okay with f2p games having mtx cosmetics as long as they don't change gameplay. Then it became I'm okay with f2p games having battlepasses since they're alll cosmetic! It slowly turned into paid games having battlepasses and shops. Now it's turning into games going up and price and still having all the mtx's in the games. Performance is getting worse, story games are getting shorter, content that should obviously be part of the base game is being cut out and made into more mtx. 

Studios are making more money than ever now. In a lot of cases the mtx revenue alone is outperforming everything else. There's no reason to justify $70 price hike. The whole inflation argument with $60 20 years ago being more than $70 today is very short sighted when you take into account how much more profitable the publishers and studios are today than 20 years ago. It's orders of magnitude in difference. All indicators point to games being cheaper than ever to produce. It's very obvious with this massive shift where AAA studios left and right are announcing moves to unreal engine over maintaining in house engines. That is a massive time + $$ save in dev hours alone.

If you still think $70 games are okay that's fine. We can agree to disagree, but I will never ever justify it because I know that games are cheaper than ever to produce, the quality of these games have been going down over the years, and they are making more money than ever by a significant degree.

